## Quick start

You need [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/). Nothing else: no key, no account, no server.

```bash
make install   # the locked environment
make build     # every seed, model, contract and test, on DuckDB
make docs      # the dbt docs site with its lineage graph, in dbt/target/static_index.html
make test      # the tests, offline
make check     # lint, format, strict types and the code standard
```

To run the DAGs through Airflow, `make install-airflow` then `make dags-test`.

## Adding a source

1. Write its dlt source and the load that runs it in `pipelines/<source>.py`, with its settings in
   `pipelines/config.py` and `config/config.toml`, and name the load in `LOADS` in
   `pipelines/__main__.py`, so `python -m pipelines load <source>` runs it.
2. Declare its raw tables in `dbt/models/staging/_<source>__sources.yml`, with freshness limits, and
   give each a staging view, `stg_<source>__<table>`.
3. Add a DAG in `dags/` that runs the load and updates an asset named for its raw schema, list the
   asset in `RAW_SCHEMAS` in `dags/defaults.py`, so the build runs after it, and add the DAG's id to
   `DAGS` in the Makefile.
4. Test it offline, on fixtures in `tests/`.

## Project layout

| Path | What it holds |
| --- | --- |
| `pipelines/` | The dlt sources and `python -m pipelines`, which the Makefile, CI and the DAGs run |
| `dbt/` | The dbt project: staging, intermediate and mart models, seeds, macros and tests ([`dbt/README.md`](dbt/README.md)) |
| `dags/` | The Airflow 3 DAGs ([`dags/README.md`](dags/README.md)) |
| `config/` | Every setting and the secrets template ([`config/README.md`](config/README.md)) |
| `tests/` | The tests, offline |
| `data/` | Only `generated/`, ignored: the warehouse, dlt's state, Airflow's home ([`data/README.md`](data/README.md)) |

